        <section id="faq" class="faq-container">
            <h2>7. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h4>What is the difference between a sanitizer and a disinfectant aerosol?</h4>
                <p>Sanitizers are designed to reduce bacterial populations to safe levels (usually 99.9%), whereas disinfectants are higher-grade chemicals designed to kill 99.999% of bacteria, viruses, and in some cases, fungi, on non-porous surfaces.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h4>Can I launch a disinfectant aerosol without CDSCO approval in India?</h4>
                <p>No. In India, surface disinfectants are regulated under the Drugs and Cosmetics Act. Launching without proper licensing can lead to significant legal penalties and product recalls.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h4>Why does my disinfectant aerosol spray 'spit' or clog?</h4>
                <p>This is usually due to improper formulation balance (e.g., solid active ingredients falling out of solution) or an incorrect combination of valve orifice size and propellant pressure.</p>
            </div>
